  "body": "## Dependency and scope\n\nDepends on #401 (atomic canonical refund accounting), which depends on #396 (refund execution fence). Merge in that order only after review; this PR does not merge or activate providers. The mobile generated-contract companion is based on mobile #82.\n\nKnown-ID recovery for existing PayPal mixing/mastering refunds only:\n\n- A bounded, environment-pinned GET adapter validates immutable refund/capture IDs, exact USD minor units and link evidence.\n- Strict-admin local-readiness and explicit-query endpoints; durable audit admission, shared query quota, role/flag/account/capability gates and authority recheck.\n- Exact completion uses the existing atomic refund/intent/ledger/receipt path. Every other outcome remains held; never creates another refund or grants another execution permit.\n- Spanish/English admin panel with exact money, explicit action, duplicate-submit protection, response binding validation, stale-result clearing and accessibility tests.\n- Canonical OpenAPI and generated web/mobile contracts; no new schema, backfill, card data or seller custody.\n\n## Evidence and current blockers\n\nRead ADR 0130 and `docs/payments/held-refund-query-2026-09-16.md` for the threat boundaries, configuration/rollback runbook, source dates and exact logs.\n\nPassed locally: **2665 backend examples**, **249 real PostgreSQL/migration examples**, **2072 web tests**, **329 mobile tests**, **234 repository-quality tests**, web/mobile typecheck, mobile lint, web build/bundle budget, and strict JSON/CSV catalog review (1438 files, 1136 candidates). The generated web/mobile contracts match exactly. Exact commands/revisions/UTC timestamps and logs are in the report.\n\nInitial DB verification found a nonexistent binding column; corrected to binding -> attempt -> checkout, then passed focused 51-case and fresh-database 249-case runs, including full completion rollback and used-history rollback rejection. Initial mobile full run failed two timing-sensitive tests; both passed in isolation and the entire 329-case suite passed unchanged. No timeout or gate was weakened.\n\nInitial hosted UI quality found an unnecessary test-only cast. The user approved its repair under the CI-repair workflow. An intermediate matcher was unavailable in this Jest setup and was replaced with the built-in DOM disabled-attribute assertion. Final affected suites pass **26/26** and targeted zero-warning lint passes. **Full GitHub web quality now passes on final head 365561aecff57e76d38cb0e98217a34f1d642ff4**: https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35130265919/job/104909571494 (observed 2026-09-16T17:56:46Z). This includes the original zero-warning lint gate, typecheck, full tests and build. Backend CI is still running; this is not an all-checks-green claim. Backend/payment runtime did not change during the assertion repair.\n\nAll provider callbacks in tests are synthetic/injected, not PayPal sandbox successes. Fresh staging metadata at 2026-09-16T17:12:20.897Z: both health endpoints respond; all six hosting metadata/secret-presence reads blocked by authentication; deployed SHA unknown, provider qualification false. No sandbox, staging deploy, production transaction or screenshot was performed.\n\n## Activation / rollback\n\nDefault off: process switch PAYPAL_REFUND_RECONCILIATION_ENABLED and exact-environment checkout.paypal.refund_reconciliation flag. Also requires qualified merchant and environment-verified server-verification/full/partial-refund capabilities. No sandbox bypass. Keep existing charge/refund flags unchanged.\n\nDisable the new switch and flag before rollback; drain requests and retain every audit/financial record. Never reissue ambiguous refunds, erase history or overwrite canonical drift. Unknown external IDs, legacy failed records, other domains/providers, seller/fee/tax allocations and regulatory/accounting qualification remain separate blockers.\n\nCompanion: https://github.com/diegueins680/TDF-mobile/pull/85, based on mobile #82. Both branches are pushed and verified draft/OPEN. No review requested or merge performed. Local disposable database clusters were stopped and their synthetic data/logs retained.\n\nFinal verification follow-up: GitHub web quality completed successfully at **2026-09-16T17:54:27Z** on head **365561aecff57e76d38cb0e98217a34f1d642ff4**. The fixed targeted 26-test run completed at 17:45:19Z; fixed targeted lint at 17:45:04Z (both exit 0). The old-source full local lint failed at 17:44:46Z with the same pre-fix cast error. A redundant final local full-lint run was stopped after GitHub's complete web gate passed (17:59:31Z, exit 143, log `/private/tmp/tdf-held-refund-lint-web-final-20260916.log`); it is **cancelled, not a local lint pass**. No checks or rules were disabled. All task-owned local test processes and disposable database servers are stopped; the worktrees are clean. Backend GitHub quality remains pending at this handoff; local backend 2665 / PostgreSQL 249 verification is separate evidence.\n",
